<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>Pactlocke third-party licences</title>
<style>
  body { font-family: system-ui, sans-serif; max-width: 60rem; margin: 2rem auto; padding: 0 1rem; line-height: 1.5; color: #1d1d1f; background: #fff; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.25rem; margin-top: 2.5rem; border-bottom: 1px solid #ddd; }
  h3 { font-size: 1.1rem; margin-top: 2rem; }
  pre { white-space: pre-wrap; background: #f5f5f7; padding: 1rem; border-radius: 6px; font-size: 0.85rem; }
  ul.crates { columns: 2; font-size: 0.9rem; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    body { color: #e8e8ea; background: #18181a; }
    pre { background: #242428; }
    h2 { border-color: #333; }
    a { color: #8ab4f8; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>Pactlocke third-party licences</h1>
<p>Pactlocke is licensed under the GNU General Public License, version 3 or
later (see LICENSE). It is built with the Rust crates below, each under its own
licence, reproduced here with the copyright notices their authors give.
The crates' own notice and copyright files, and the licences of the fonts egui
builds in, are in the licences/crates folder. NOTICE.md lists the rest: mGBA
(licences/mGBA-MPL-2.0.txt) and the inih (licences/inih-BSD-3-Clause.txt) and
public-domain LZMA SDK code built into it.</p>

<h2>Overview</h2>
<ul>
{{#each overview}}
  <li><a href="#{{id}}">{{name}}</a> ({{count}})</li>
{{/each}}
</ul>

<h2>Licence texts</h2>
{{#each licenses}}
<h3 id="{{id}}">{{name}}</h3>
<p>Used by:</p>
<ul class="crates">
{{#each used_by}}
  <li><a href="{{#if crate.repository}}{{crate.repository}}{{else}}https://crates.io/crates/{{crate.name}}{{/if}}">{{crate.name}} {{crate.version}}</a></li>
{{/each}}
</ul>
<pre>{{text}}</pre>
{{/each}}
</body>
</html>
